 "answer": "I can't give you a reliable live reading. The search tool only returns cached snapshots of air quality pages, and they disagree with each other.\n\n- **IQAir (Pontianak city):** The snapshot showed a US AQI of 227, which is \"Very unhealthy\". PM2.5 was 152 µg/m³. It was stamped 18:00 local time on Oct 15, and the page was about a week old.\n- **AQICN:** It showed an AQI of 62, which is \"Moderate\", driven by PM2.5.\n- **IQAir (Pontianak Barat district):** The snapshot showed an AQI of 53, \"Moderate\". It was stamped Feb 10.\n- **Weather Underground:** Its snapshot said \"Hazardous\".\n\nPontianak's air quality swings a lot with the seasons. Peat and forest fire smoke from the dry season (roughly August to October) can push PM2.5 into the unhealthy range. Outside those months it's usually moderate. The 227 reading fits that smoke pattern, and the Moderate readings fit the other months.\n\nFor the current number, check these directly:\n- iqair.com/air-quality/indonesia/west-kalimantan/pontianak\n- aqicn.org/city/indonesia/pontianak\n- The Indonesian BMKG or the KLHK ISPU site\n\nIf the AQI is above 150, it's sensible to limit outdoor activity and wear an N95/KN95 mask outside. Sensitive groups should take extra care.",
